fact WorkItem(id: "WI-354", description: some(value: "Proposal: relations/rules inside an operation declaration (option B of docs/design/modify-effect-derive.md §'Where flow facts live'). Today operation_clause is only requires/ensures/effects + optional = body + meta_block — there is NO fact/rule form inside an operation, so per-op relational annotations (e.g. the Modify-effect flow facts for opaque FFI ops with no body and no defining laws) must be written top-level with fully-qualified names (foldLeft.f.a ...), which is too verbose to use. Propose a small grammar addition: an in-operation block reusing the rule_body term grammar so edges are written with BARE params in scope (e.g. flow direct(z, f.a), element_of(xs, f.t)), co-located with the op and closer to the stdlib op-plus-sibling-laws idiom; lowers to the same top-level facts the loader derives. Must NOT overload ensures (runtime postcondition, different semantics). Alternative considered: option A, a flow-specific compact table (narrower, bespoke). SCOPE: write the proposal (grammar form, scoping rules with op.param projection in scope, lowering). ERGONOMICS-ONLY and DEFERRED — native ops + law-specified ops cover the stdlib without it (see WI-352). Depends on op.param projection."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-351"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
